<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Chicken-Thursday.jpg" alt="A portrait of a white chicken seen from the side in a brown-gray setting." width="450" height="462" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Chicken Thursday. approx. 16" x 16" oil on linen. Unmounted. 2014.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The latest painting off the easel. &nbsp;It is currently unmounted so there are a few natural hills and valleys in the surface of the linen which you can see in this image.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This is one of the chickens I photographed last weekend at George's Mill. I am particularly fond of all the non-chicken parts of this painting, although they were, by far, the hardest parts to paint. &nbsp;I established the foreground texture by layering green paint over an impressionistic block in. &nbsp;The background is a mix of ultramarine, red and yellow - with the proportions of each varied to produce an orange, green or purple bias as required.</p>